        "original_id": "6a33b04b-c22f-53dc-b431-eddcf0cebde3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: APB, Sleeper\n- People: Louise Wener\n- Places: Scotland, London\n- Genres: post-punk, funk rock, punk rock, new wave, Britpop\n- Works: Trainspotting\n\nFacts:\n- APB was a Scottish post-punk band formed in 1979 that blended funk rock, punk rock, and new wave music.\n- During its brief run, APB achieved only modest success.\n- APB influenced the sound of later bands including Franz Ferdinand, The Rapture, and Red Hot Chili Peppers.\n- Sleeper is an English Britpop band formed in London and fronted by Louise Wener.\n- During the 1990s, Sleeper had eight UK Top 40 hit singles and three UK Top 10 albums.\n- Sleeper's music was featured on the soundtrack of the film Trainspotting.",
